      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for this, it's a good start. However, I just checked the preview in the auditor's tool and the thoroughness score is actually quite low because the heading count is too small. \n\nThe tool is looking for a really granular breakdown to prove we aren't glossing over anything. Could you expand this out? Honestly, just use more headings to break up the content. Even if a section is just one sentence or a single requirement, give it its own heading. It's better to have way more headings than to risk a low score. \n\nAlso, please don't just repeat the same thing—make sure the headings are distinct so the tool doesn't flag it as duplicate content, but definitely increase the density of the structure. Can you try again with a much higher heading count?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
